@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# GitHub delivery health — source acceptance contract
+
+Build: coordination.9-delivery-health, on the reconstructed v4.7.14 checkpoint.
+No host installation, login, provider call or task replay is performed by this
+increment. Only the existing PM writer consumes the GitHub queue.
+
+## Feedback implemented
+
+App Dev's apparently idle setup and absent local listeners: the read-only
+setup report and board expose the actual coordinator host/install/port/PID/boot.
+The launcher explains its foreground supervision and no longer points to a
+deleted Recipient pairing pane. Missing actor routes remain explicit; Devs
+still publish packets on GitHub without installing Orch.
+
+CLI Dev's live-board error and queued messages: a new delivery card joins the
+latest event to its native PM queue row by activity AND delivery identity,
+separates queued/invocation/response from receipt/result, exposes the preceding
+failed PM delivery/error, and names blocked execution rather than negotiation.
+Read-only health does not reset an errored worker or replay an uncertain action.
+
+The legacy `github_watch_last_wake` key is retained for compatibility, but the
+UI calls it “Last event queued (not wake)”. It is never used as receipt proof.
+The latest event/delivery join is durable across restart and coalescing; the
+report identifies whether it originated on the current boot. Invalid/missing
+trace identity is reported as unproven, never matched by timestamp proximity.
+
+## Evidence and limits
+
+Python tests exercise real temporary SQLite queue/settings state and stubbed
+runtime configuration. The Node smoke executes the actual dashboard JavaScript
+with a DOM stand-in, including escaped worker errors and failed-delivery IDs.
+Neither is a signed-in Mac wake, browser layout proof or provider observation.
+
+Native PM currently has a returned-response/checkpoint protocol, not a separate
+task-bound authenticated recipient ACK protocol. `end_to_end_proven` therefore
+stays false; this increment does not fabricate a green coordination receipt.
+It also does not implement callback compatibility upgrades, recover the
+unobserved installed PM subprocess error, or finish sleep/compaction recovery.
+
+## Installed acceptance still required
+
+1. Capture the actual coordinator identity and existing worker error. Reconcile
+   process ownership and any uncertain side-effect journal before recovery.
+2. Recover the sole intended PM worker through supported controls. Preserve
+   original event/delivery IDs, queue cursor and prior completed dispositions.
+3. A fresh Dev GitHub packet must create the matching delivery, invoke the
+   intended idle PM, return a task/head-matching ACK and result, and advance the
+   review without PO relay. A process, queue item or response alone is not this
+   evidence. Repeat after supported restart and sleep/re-arm.
+4. Only then accept installed coordination. Browser PM remains unavailable
+   for automatic wake until a supported inbound route is separately established.
+
+No generic reset button or blind installer restart is introduced. Diagnosis
+and recovery must preserve the one-writer and no-side-effect-replay boundaries.
